chmod
Usage: chmod [-Rcvf] MODE[,MODE]... FILE...

Change file permissions (mode) for FILE.

MODE is octal number (bit pattern sstrwxrwxrwx) or [ugoa]{+|-|=}[rwxXst]

Octal: one digit per set -- you, your group, everyone else -- and each
digit is `r`=4 plus `w`=2 plus `x`=1 added up. So `600` is read+write for
you and nothing for anyone else, `644` is `rw-r--r--`, `755` is
`rwxr-xr-x`, `700` is `rwx------`. A fourth digit in front is setuid,
setgid and sticky: `4755` runs as its owner, `1777` is a shared
directory only owners can delete from.

Symbolic: who, then what to do, then which bits. `u` is you, `g` your
group, `o` others, `a` all three; `+` adds, `-` removes, `=` sets exactly.
So `u+x` makes it executable by you, `go-w` takes write off everyone else,
`a=r` leaves it read-only for all.

	-R	Recurse
	-c	List changed files
	-v	Verbose
	-f	Hide errors
